From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui, engine: crash recovery opens a Document Recovery task pane, not a full page; local time; untitled copies named in the UI language

WP23 usability finding (owner, 2026-10-29): after a crash Docs opened File > Recover over the whole window (black page, raw ISO UTC time, plain white buttons, near-invisible headers), covering the document just double-clicked; the unsaved copy was named "Untitled draft" in English. Now a start with copies not yet offered opens the document as usual and shows a "Document Recovery" pane on the left, as Word does: the app's name from the overlay, one card per copy (name that restores on click or Enter, "Version created from the last AutoSave", time in local time as dd.mm.yyyy HH:MM, Open and Discard...), and Close. The pane marks the copies offered when shown (0129 unchanged). File > Recover keeps the list, now on the normal backstage background with the same cards. The engine stores an empty name for an untitled document; the UI shows the translated "Document1" (old copies holding "Untitled draft" map to it too). The local time comes from the new `crates/local-stamp` (ours; the one OS call lives there, the app crates keep forbidding unsafe code); the web build shows UTC.
